Package: decisionfacets
Title: Decision Accuracy and Consistency for Rater-Mediated Exams
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Daniel", "Edi", email = "danieledi2026@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Answers "would this candidate have passed with a different set
    of raters?" for rater-mediated exams such as oral examinations,
    objective structured clinical examinations and essay scoring. Builds on
    the many-facet Rasch rating scale model to compute counterfactual pass
    probabilities under the observed, an average-severity and a random rater
    panel, under an explicit decision rule (raw total, fair average or
    measure), and splits expected misclassification into measurement error
    and rater assignment. Models can be fitted with 'TAM' or a built-in joint
    maximum likelihood estimator.
